00:36:14.290 --> 00:36:16.930
And they served it, like, hot and melted and kind of gooey.
他们上菜的时候，还是热乎乎、半融化、黏糊糊的。

751
00:36:17.050 --> 00:36:17.330
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

752
00:36:17.710 --> 00:36:19.270
It was so good.
太好吃了。

753
00:36:19.490 --> 00:36:25.510
You guys, the chocolate chip cookie cake was Steve Carell's, like, kryptonite?
伙计们，巧克力豆曲奇蛋糕简直是史蒂夫·卡瑞尔的“氪星石”，对吧？

754
00:36:25.570 --> 00:36:25.730
Yes.
没错。

755
00:36:25.730 --> 00:36:26.150
I don't know.
我不知道。

756
00:36:26.270 --> 00:36:31.350
This guy would eat so healthy, but he had to eat this chocolate chip cookie cake.
这家伙平时吃得特别健康，但唯独对这巧克力豆曲奇蛋糕毫无抵抗力。

757
00:36:31.370 --> 00:36:32.310
This is one treat.
这算是一种犒劳。

758
00:36:32.690 --> 00:36:34.450
But literally, they said they didn't think much about it.
但说真的，他们说当时也没多想。

759
00:36:34.490 --> 00:36:35.170
They made it one time.
他们就做了一次。

760
00:36:35.290 --> 00:36:36.290
And then everyone was like, where is it?
然后大家都在问，蛋糕呢？

761
00:36:36.330 --> 00:36:36.670
Where is it?
蛋糕去哪了？

762
00:36:36.770 --> 00:36:38.030
They had to make it, like, every day.
结果他们不得不每天都做。

763
00:36:38.170 --> 00:36:38.370
Yeah.
是啊。

764
00:36:38.850 --> 00:36:41.350
So now I have to talk about Peter and Vartan.
现在我得聊聊彼得和瓦尔坦了。

765
00:36:41.590 --> 00:36:43.090
They were the snack masters.
他们是片场的零食大师。

766
00:36:43.750 --> 00:36:47.970
They had kind of like a full kitchen right on the set, right outside the Dunder Mifflin
他们在片场直接搭了个完整的厨房，就在邓德·米夫林公司

767
00:36:47.970 --> 00:36:48.410
bullpen.
办公区外面。

768
00:36:48.670 --> 00:36:48.870
Yep.
没错。

769
00:36:49.130 --> 00:36:50.150
You know, they had a fridge.
你知道，他们有个冰箱。

770
00:36:50.290 --> 00:36:51.070
You could have cereal.
你可以吃麦片。

771
00:36:51.230 --> 00:36:51.790
They had milk.
他们有牛奶。

772
00:36:51.930 --> 00:36:53.110
You could make your own sandwich.
你可以自己做三明治。

773
00:36:53.150 --> 00:36:55.930
But they would also have a little food bar.
但他们还会准备一个小食吧。

774
00:36:56.010 --> 00:36:57.450
And here's what they had to share.
以下是他们准备分享的东西。

775
00:36:58.110 --> 00:37:00.690
Peter talked about how he had been in the business forever.
彼得说他已经在这一行干了很久了。

776
00:37:01.130 --> 00:37:06.470
He also said, I thought this was kind of funny, that our cast, we were tea obsessed.
他还说了一件我觉得挺逗的事，他说我们剧组的人对茶特别痴迷。

777
00:37:06.470 --> 00:37:09.090
He had hundreds of different types of teas.
他有几百种不同的茶。

778
00:37:10.850 --> 00:37:15.290
And you might have noticed that I didn't make Sergio and Alan's breakfast liSt.
你们可能注意到了，我没把塞尔吉奥和艾伦列入早餐名单。

779
00:37:15.450 --> 00:37:17.890
Because you would never eat an egg in the morning.
因为你早上根本不会吃鸡蛋。

780
00:37:18.270 --> 00:37:21.330
Because Peter and Vartan got donuts every morning.
因为彼得和瓦尔坦每天早上都会买甜甜圈。

781
00:37:21.870 --> 00:37:24.770
So I would go get a donut from Peter and Vartan.
所以我都会去彼得和瓦尔坦那儿拿个甜甜圈。

782
00:37:25.010 --> 00:37:27.970
Also, BJ liked the Porto's coffee cake.
另外，BJ喜欢波尔图咖啡蛋糕。

783
00:37:28.350 --> 00:37:31.990
And then Peter said, sometimes he would make you and I sandwiches.
然后彼得说，有时候他会为你和我做三明治。

784
00:37:32.310 --> 00:37:32.850
He would.
他确实会做。

785
00:37:33.070 --> 00:37:35.450
And he said he loved doing it.
他说他很乐意做这些。

786
00:37:35.450 --> 00:37:38.850
And he would put them on a porcelain plate and bring them to us.
他会把三明治放在瓷盘上，然后端给我们。

787
00:37:39.050 --> 00:37:39.690
I'm crying again.
我又想哭了。

788
00:37:39.930 --> 00:37:40.450
I know.
我知道。

789
00:37:40.730 --> 00:37:41.450
I know.
我懂。

790
00:37:41.590 --> 00:37:43.270
He took such good care of us.
他把我们照顾得太好了。

791
00:37:43.930 --> 00:37:45.690
I can't explain to you.
我没法向你们解释。

792
00:37:46.830 --> 00:37:51.010
Like the care with which he would make us a sandwich.
就是他为我们做三明治时那种用心的程度。

793
00:37:51.050 --> 00:37:52.590
It's so silly and simple.
听起来很傻、很简单。

794
00:37:52.750 --> 00:37:53.470
But he would.
但他真的会那么做。

795
00:37:53.610 --> 00:37:55.170
He'd put it on a porcelain plate.
他会把它放在瓷盘上。

796
00:37:55.170 --> 00:38:00.330
And he'd always like garnish it with some cute little like fruit or like a little pickles.
而且他总是会用可爱的小水果或者小酸黄瓜之类的来装饰一下。

797
00:38:00.330 --> 00:38:01.970
Like he'd cut fruit into a shape.
就像他会把水果切成某种形状一样。

798
00:38:02.130 --> 00:38:02.350
Yeah.
是啊。

799
00:38:02.630 --> 00:38:03.630
It really was.
确实如此。

800
00:38:03.730 --> 00:38:05.450
It was like your grandpa made you a sandwich.
就像是你爷爷亲手为你做三明治一样。

801
00:38:05.450 --> 00:38:06.270
It really was.
确实如此。

802
00:38:06.410 --> 00:38:07.770
And you felt so loved.
而且你感觉被深深地爱着。

803
00:38:07.850 --> 00:38:09.510
He was so happy to do it.
他做这些事非常开心。

804
00:38:09.590 --> 00:38:09.750
Yeah.
是啊。

805
00:38:09.870 --> 00:38:12.150
He said that he would make you a tuna fish sandwich.
他说他会给你做一个金枪鱼三明治。

806
00:38:12.150 --> 00:38:14.290
And he'd make me ham and cheese.
然后他会给我做火腿芝士三明治。

807
00:38:14.570 --> 00:38:16.550
I cried through this commentary, Jenna.
珍娜，听这段评论音轨时我全程都在哭。

808
00:38:16.710 --> 00:38:22.470
I laughed so hard because Peter and Vartan give each other like such a hard time lovingly.
我笑得特别厉害，因为彼得和瓦尔坦总是那样充满爱意地互相调侃。

809
00:38:22.730 --> 00:38:23.510
And they're so funny.
他们真的太搞笑了。

810
00:38:24.150 --> 00:38:26.170
Alan called them the Middle Eastern odd couple.
艾伦管他们叫“中东版的老友记”。

811
00:38:26.890 --> 00:38:30.290
Because Peter is from Greece and Vartan is from Iraq.
因为彼得来自希腊，而瓦尔坦来自伊拉克。

812
00:38:30.630 --> 00:38:33.150
They had a hilarious banter, the two of them.
他们俩的斗嘴简直太逗了。

813
00:38:33.350 --> 00:38:37.470
They also talked about their infamous 10 a.m.
他们还聊到了他们那臭名昭著的上午十点钟

814
00:38:37.710 --> 00:38:38.450
hot snack.
热乎零食。

815
00:38:38.710 --> 00:38:39.410
Hot snack.
热乎零食。

816
00:38:39.410 --> 00:38:40.650
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

817
00:38:40.970 --> 00:38:42.770
Peter said they like to mix it up every day.
彼得说他们喜欢每天换着花样吃。

818
00:38:43.010 --> 00:38:45.710
He said on Mondays, for example, there'd be tacos and burritos.
他说比如周一，会有塔可饼和墨西哥卷饼。

819
00:38:46.230 --> 00:38:49.090
One of the most popular hot snack items was.
最受欢迎的热乎零食之一是

820
00:38:49.850 --> 00:38:50.610
Albandegas soup.
阿尔邦迪加斯汤。

821
00:38:51.190 --> 00:38:53.790
Well, they talked about that, but they said their turkey chili.
嗯，他们聊到了那个，但他们说他们的火鸡辣椒酱

822
00:38:54.370 --> 00:38:54.770
Oh.
哦。

823
00:38:55.190 --> 00:38:58.090
They said their turkey chili they had to serve twice a week.
他们说火鸡辣椒酱他们每周得供应两次。

824
00:38:58.310 --> 00:38:59.150
People wanted it.
大家都想要。

825
00:38:59.370 --> 00:38:59.970
They loved it.
他们超爱那个。

826
00:39:00.370 --> 00:39:03.130
Ed Helms, in particular, loved the turkey chili.
尤其是艾德·赫尔姆斯，特别爱吃火鸡辣椒酱。

827
00:39:03.270 --> 00:39:04.890
And he came up with a little tip.
而且他还想出了一个小妙招。

828
00:39:05.050 --> 00:39:05.690
What is it?
是什么？

829
00:39:05.850 --> 00:39:08.330
Ed, you know, they had garnishes on the side for the chili.
艾德，你知道的，他们会给辣椒酱配上配菜。

830
00:39:08.330 --> 00:39:10.810
They had shredded cheese and they had onions.
有碎芝士和洋葱。

831
00:39:11.090 --> 00:39:16.410
Ed would put the raw onions at the bottom of his bowl, add the hot turkey chili on top,
艾德会把生洋葱放在碗底，然后把热乎的火鸡辣椒酱倒在上面，

832
00:39:16.450 --> 00:39:19.310
and the heat from the chili would caramelize the onions at the bottom.
辣椒酱的热度就会把底部的洋葱焖得焦香。

833
00:39:19.550 --> 00:39:19.770
Wow.
哇。

834
00:39:20.110 --> 00:39:21.210
It became a thing.
这成了一个招牌吃法。

835
00:39:22.670 --> 00:39:31.850
So, and much like our Dunder Mifflin counterparts, they said the cast and crew had their favorite pizza places to order from if we went to overtime.
所以，就像我们《办公室》剧组一样，他们说如果加班的话，演职人员都有自己最爱点的披萨店。

836
00:39:32.030 --> 00:39:33.310
And we got second meal.
然后我们就会吃第二顿饭。

837
00:39:33.910 --> 00:39:35.550
Steve loved Mulberry's pizza.
史蒂夫最爱吃桑树披萨。

838
00:39:36.210 --> 00:39:38.330
And we all loved Baroni's pizza.
而我们所有人都爱吃巴罗尼披萨。

839
00:39:38.630 --> 00:39:38.950
Yes.
没错。

840
00:39:39.190 --> 00:39:40.890
It was a delight, you guys.
伙计们，那真是太棒了。

841
00:39:40.890 --> 00:39:43.630
I just have to tell you, we loved these men so much.
我必须得告诉你们，我们真的太爱这几位男士了。

842
00:39:43.810 --> 00:39:48.530
I was lucky enough to work with Sergio again when I guest starred on Mindy's show, Never Have I Ever.
我有幸在客串明迪的剧集《好想做一次》时再次与塞尔吉奥合作。

843
00:39:48.710 --> 00:39:50.930
She still wants Sergio on her projects.
她现在依然想让塞尔吉奥参与她的项目。

844
00:39:50.930 --> 00:39:51.970
It was so awesome.
那真是太棒了。

845
00:39:52.230 --> 00:39:53.630
These guys were our family.
这些人就是我们的家人。

846
00:39:54.010 --> 00:39:54.450
Yeah.
是啊。

847
00:39:54.810 --> 00:39:56.370
And they took such good care of us.
他们把我们照顾得太好了。

848
00:39:56.370 --> 00:40:03.530
And if you have ever wondered why the only thing my dad talked about was the food when he visited set, listen to this commentary.
如果你曾经好奇为什么我爸爸来片场探班时，嘴里念叨的只有吃的，那就听听这段评论音轨吧。

849
00:40:03.970 --> 00:40:05.010
I loved that.
我喜欢那个。

850
00:40:05.210 --> 00:40:06.310
I loved it, too.
我也很喜欢。

851
00:40:06.470 --> 00:40:09.130
And I know I went on and on, but I had to share it.
我知道我说了又说，但我必须分享一下。

852
00:40:09.230 --> 00:40:13.050
I hope everyone else found it interesting because I loved that trip down memory lane.
希望其他人也觉得很有趣，因为我很喜欢那段回忆之旅。

853
00:40:13.250 --> 00:40:13.930
Thank you, Angela.
谢谢你，安吉拉。

854
00:40:14.110 --> 00:40:14.730
You're welcome.
不客气。

855
00:40:15.450 --> 00:40:15.890
All right.
好了。

856
00:40:16.330 --> 00:40:17.530
Should we get into this episode?
我们要开始聊这一集了吗？

857
00:40:17.750 --> 00:40:18.730
I guess we can.
我想我们可以开始了。

858
00:40:19.090 --> 00:40:20.670
I will pull myself together.
我会调整好状态的。

859
00:40:21.030 --> 00:40:21.390
Yes.
好的。

860
00:40:26.510 --> 00:40:30.810
Pam is kind of mad because nobody congratulated her on her engagement.
帕姆有点生气，因为没人祝贺她订婚。

861
00:40:31.630 --> 00:40:33.530
And Jim says, yeah, I didn't tell anyone.
吉姆说，是的，我没告诉任何人。

862
00:40:34.830 --> 00:40:36.870
And then he's like, let's tell him.
然后他说，我们告诉他吧。

863
00:40:37.010 --> 00:40:38.690
And he puts Pam on speakerphone.
于是他把帕姆的电话开了免提。

864
00:40:38.750 --> 00:40:41.570
And it goes, I think exactly how Jim thought it would go.
结果正如吉姆所料。

865
00:40:42.070 --> 00:40:42.330
Yeah.
没错。

866
00:40:42.530 --> 00:40:47.110
It ends with Michael arriving and hearing the news and tackling Jim to the floor.
最后迈克尔赶到，听到了这个消息，然后把吉姆扑倒在地。

